independentExercise.solution:
```cpp
// C++17
void report(const Quote& q) {
    std::visit([](const auto& alt) {
        using T = std::decay_t<decltype(alt)>;
        if constexpr (std::is_same_v<T, Price>) std::cout << "px " << alt.value << "\n";
        else                                    std::cout << "miss " << alt.why << "\n";
    }, q);
}
```

Exact output for the stream:

```
px 100.25
miss halt
px 101.5
```

`std::visit` dispatches to the same generic lambda with `alt` bound to `const Price&` for quotes 1 and 3 and `const Missing&` for quote 2; `if constexpr` compiles a different branch per alternative, so the variant's state - not a flag - decides the line printed.

